<title>USA: USDA says Italy, Czech free of two animal diseases.</title>
<headline>USDA says Italy, Czech free of two animal diseases.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday said it has declared Italy and the Czech Republic free of rinderpest and food-and-mouth disease and plans to change import rules.</p>
<p>USDA said it would publish a final rule in the Federal Register on October 4 that would allow the import of live ruminants and fresh, chilled, and frozen meat ruminants and lift curbs on imports of ruminant milk and milk products from the two countries.</p>
<p>USDA said in July it was proposing to declare the two nations rid of the animal diseases.</p>
</text>
